---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
import { COMPETITIONS } from '../config/competitions';
---
<Base title="About" description="Who we are, and where every table and headline on Panenka Goal comes from.">
  <article class="wrap module prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Football talk, in Kannada</h1>
    <p lang="kn" class="kn" style="font-size:20px">{SITE.taglineKn}</p>
    <p>
      Panenka Goal is a fan-made channel covering Indian football, Karnataka football, youth football and women's football,
      mainly in Kannada. This site collects our shows, the tables that matter to us, and the day's headlines in one place.
    </p>

    <h2>Where the data comes from</h2>
    <ul>
      {COMPETITIONS.map((c) => <li><b>{c.name}:</b> <a href={c.sourceUrl} rel="noopener">{c.sourceLabel}</a></li>)}
      <li><b>Videos:</b> our YouTube channel and the official MG Indian Super League channel. Videos play from YouTube.</li>
      <li><b>News:</b> Indian football headlines from the public feeds of KhelNow, The Hindu, Times of India and Deccan Herald, plus posts from official accounts. We show the headline and a one-line summary, and every item links to the original article.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We fetch each source a few times a day at most and credit it on every table. If you run one of these sources and want
      something changed or removed, message us on <a href={SITE.socials.instagram} rel="noopener">Instagram</a> and we will act on it.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">Our fetcher identifies itself as <code>PanenkaGoalBot</code>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose { max-width: 72ch; display: grid; gap: 14px; }
  .prose h2 { margin-top: 12px; }
  ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 20px; display: grid; gap: 4px; }
</style>
